<% layout('layout/boilerplate.ejs') %>

<main>
  <section class="section container">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">&larr; Back</a>

    <div class="feature-card">
      <div class="feature-card-header">
        <span class="feature-card-dot"></span>
        <span class="feature-card-dot"></span>
        <span class="feature-card-dot"></span>
        <span class="title">dx — voult.dev</span>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-card-body">
        <div class="feature-full">
          <h1>Smooth DX, easy integration</h1>
          <p class="feature-full-intro">
            Adding authentication should feel like a natural extension of your project, not a multi-day detour. We obsess over the developer experience so you don't have to.
          </p>

          <h2>What's included</h2>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Drop-in integration</strong> — add voult to an existing Express, Next.js, or Vite app in minutes. Our CLI generates the config files and initial setup for you.</li>
            <li><strong>Sensible defaults</strong> — secure settings are the default. You don't need a security background to get started.</li>
            <li><strong>Escape hatches when you need them</strong> — every layer is configurable. Override session behavior, swap token strategies, plug in custom OAuth providers.</li>
            <li><strong>Works with your stack</strong> — adapters are available for Express, Next.js API routes, Vite, and plain Node.js. More frameworks are on the way.</li>
            <li><strong>Local development friendly</strong> — the CLI spins up a local auth server or proxies to a test project so you can build without cloud credentials.</li>
          </ul>

          <p>
            If you've ever stared at a 40-step auth tutorial wondering why something this common is this hard—we feel your pain. That's exactly why voult exists.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>
